lectrical property measurement products. It also provides etch, plasma dicing, deposition and other wafer processing technologies and solutions; direct imaging, inspection, optical shaping, inkjet, and additive printing, as well as computer-aided manufacturing and engineering solutions; and components. In addition, the company offers service programs. It serves semiconductor, and semiconductor-related and electronic device manufacturers. The company operates in China, Taiwan, Korea, North America, Japan, Europe, Israel, and rest of Asia. The company was formerly known as KLA-Tencor Corporation and changed its name to KLA Corporation in July 2019. KLA Corporation was incorporated in 1975 and is headquartered in Milpitas, California.","employees":17000,"website":"https://www.kla.com","country":"United States","city":"Milpitas","officers":[{"name":"Mr. Richard P. Wallace","title":"President, CEO & Executive Director"},{"name":"Mr. Bren D. Higgins","title":"Executive VP & CFO"},{"name":"Ms. Mary Beth Wilkinson","title":"Executive VP, Chief Legal Officer & Corporate Secretary"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":18.39,"tpe":32.71,"ps":6.516,"pfcf":32.14,"peg":1.005,"pb":7.933,"rev_growth":0.215,"eps_growth":0.4515,"eps_growth_fwd":0.2552,"eps_growth_next":0.1933,"div_yield":0.0011,"roe":0.2323,"roa":0.07977,"de":47.91,"gross_margin":0.5924,"op_margin":0.225,"profit_margin":0.1914,"current_ratio":1.554},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":21.6,"sector":18.39,"score":0,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":39.78,"sector":32.71,"score":0,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":13.99,"sector":6.516,"score":-1,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":72.4,"sector":32.14,"score":-1,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"peg","label":"PEG","v":1.39,"sector":1.005,"score":null,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"pb","label":"Price / Book","v":29.97,"sector":7.933,"score":null,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"de","label":"Deb